    "instructions": "Write `filter_primes(numbers: list[int]) -> list[int]` returning prime numbers (> 1) from the list in order.",
    "starter_code": "def filter_primes(numbers: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    pass\n",
    "solution_code": "def filter_primes(numbers: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    def is_p(n):\n        if n < 2:\n            return False\n        for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n            if n % i == 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n    return [n for n in numbers if is_p(n)]\n",
